From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: appcommands: fix size_t underflow in convertIntelVersion for single-digit major

convertIntelVersion() does:
    majorVer.substr(majorVer.size() - 2)
to take the last two digits of the major version field.  When the major
version is a single character (e.g. "0" from "onetree-0.0-0-gXXX-YYY"),
size() - 2 underflows to SIZE_T_MAX = npos, and substr(npos) throws
std::out_of_range: "basic_string::substr: __pos (4294967295) > this->size()".

ipmid catches this as "Handler failed to catch exception" on every Get
Device ID call, returning 0xFF to netipmid, which returns 0xFF to
ipmitool.  ipmitool treats this as a fatal session error and drops the
IPMI SOL session.

Fix: if the major version string is shorter than 2 chars, use it as-is.

--- a/src/appcommands.cpp
+++ b/src/appcommands.cpp
@@ -240,8 +240,9 @@ std::optional<MetaRevision> convertIntelVersion(std::string& s)
             rev.platform = results[1];
             std::string majorVer = results[2].str();
             // Take only the last two digits of the major version
-            rev.major = static_cast<uint8_t>(
-                std::stoi(majorVer.substr(majorVer.size() - 2)));
+            rev.major = static_cast<uint8_t>(std::stoi(
+                majorVer.size() >= 2 ? majorVer.substr(majorVer.size() - 2)
+                                     : majorVer));
             rev.minor = static_cast<uint8_t>(std::stoi(results[3]));
             rev.buildNo = static_cast<uint32_t>(std::stoi(results[4]));
             rev.openbmcHash = results[6];
